---
// src/pages/hollywood/swarm/index.astro · 0825 V1
// The Signature in the Swarm — the fly-god page under Studios & Genre.
//
// This is a genre hub, not a study: it names Baal-zebub, states the doctrinal
// test every entry is measured by, and lists the films. The entries live in
// src/data/hollywood.js on the `swarm` card; adding a film is a data edit plus
// its page, nothing here.
//
// Built in Astro rather than as static HTML under public/hollywood/films, where
// its Studios siblings still sit. That legacy sub-site carries its own <head>,
// its own breadcrumb and its own stylesheet, so those pages get no site header,
// no theme, no social card and no search indexing. New work goes on the stack.
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { swarm, swarmEntries } from '../../../data/hollywood.js';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Signature in the Swarm — Hollywood | Nazaryah"
  description={swarm.description}
>
<div class="craft-shell">
<main class="wrap">
  <p class="eyebrow">Studios &amp; Genre — Hollywood</p>
  <h1>The Signature in the Swarm</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Hollywood keeps reaching for the same insect. Scripture named him first.</p>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <h2>The Name</h2>
  <p>
    Ahaziah, king of Israel, fell through a lattice and was badly hurt. He sent men to
    ask Baal-zebub, the god of Ekron, whether he would live. Yahuah sent Elijah to meet
    them on the road with one question — is there not a God in Israel? — and one
    sentence. The king would not come down off that bed.
  </p>
  <blockquote>
    <p>
      Is it not because there is not a God in Israel, that ye go to enquire of
      Baal-zebub the god of Ekron?
    </p>
    <cite>2 Kings 1:2-4</cite>
  </blockquote>
  <p>
    He did not build the fly-god a temple. He did not sacrifice to him. He asked him a
    question. That was enough.
  </p>
  <p>
    Baal-zebub means lord of the fly. The name returns in the gospels, spelled
    Beelzebub, as the title of the prince of devils (Matthew 12:24).
  </p>

  <h2>The Doctrine</h2>
  <p>Every film under this page turns on one question. Where does evil live?</p>
  <p>
    Scripture answers plainly. Sin is the transgression of the law (1 John 3:4). A
    broken command. A charge on a record. Not a substance in the flesh, not a residue
    in the meat, not an atmosphere a sensitive person can feel in a room.
  </p>
  <p>
    If sin is a substance, it comes out by technique — a gifted man, a method, a
    transfer. No law, no court, no judge. That is sorcery.
  </p>
  <p>
    If sin is a charge, it comes out by verdict — a standard, a witness, a sentence,
    and blood (Hebrews 9:22). That is Scripture.
  </p>

  <h2>Two Lies, One Root</h2>
  <ul class="lies">
    <li>The evil is inside you and can never be removed. That one ends in despair.</li>
    <li>The evil is inside you and a gifted man can draw it out. That one ends in sorcery.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    They look like opposites. They are not. Both put sin in the flesh instead of on the
    record, and once that is settled neither one needs a law and neither one needs blood.
  </p>

  <h2>Why an Insect</h2>
  <p>
    Flies gather where something has died. They announce death. They do not explain it.
  </p>
  <p>
    That is what makes the swarm useful. It tells an audience something is wrong here
    without ever naming a broken command, a lawbreaker, or a price. It is guilt with the
    courtroom stripped out — carrying a devil's name the audience is never told.
  </p>

  <h2>How to Read the Entries</h2>
  <p>Each film below gets the same three questions.</p>
  <ol class="tests">
    <li>Where does the story say the evil lives?</li>
    <li>How does the story remove it?</li>
    <li>Who pays, and by what standard?</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="close">The third question is where every one of them falls silent.</p>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <h2 class="entries-head">The Entries</h2>
  <ul class="entries" role="list">
    {swarmEntries.map((e) => (
      <li class={`entry ${e.status}`}>
        <a href={e.href} class={`entry-link ${e.status === 'live' ? '' : 'is-coming'}`}>
          <span class="entry-n">{String(e.n).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
          <span class="entry-body">
            <span class="entry-title">{e.title}</span>
            <span class="entry-work">{e.work}</span>
            <span class="entry-tag">{e.tagline}</span>
            <span class="entry-verses">{e.verses}</span>
          </span>
          {e.status === 'live'
            ? <span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            : <span class="entry-soon">In production</span>}
        </a>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <p class="back-wrap"><a class="back" href="/hollywood">← Back to Hollywood</a></p>

  <hr class="rule" />
  <footer class="craft-footer">nazaryah.com</footer>
</main>
</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* The Hollywood house theme, scoped to this shell so it never leaks to the
     global header/footer. Same palette as The Craft and The Stars. */
  .craft-shell {
    --bg: #160a0c;
    --bg-raise: #201114;
    --ink: #ece1cd;
    --ink-soft: #b6a58f;
    --parchment: #ecd8a6;
    --gold: #c99a44;
    --gold-soft: #a98a53;
    --rule: rgba(201, 154, 68, 0.22);
    --display: "Cormorant Garamond", Georgia, serif;
    --body: "EB Garamond", Georgia, serif;
    --maxw: 46rem;

    background:
      radial-gradient(120% 80% at 50% -10%, #241318 0%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0) 55%),
      radial-gradient(140% 120% at 50% 0%, #1d1012 0%, var(--bg) 60%);
    background-color: var(--bg);
    min-height: 80vh;
  }

  .wrap {
    max-width: var(--maxw);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: clamp(2.6rem, 7vw, 5.5rem) 1.4rem 4rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--body);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variant-caps: small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.32em;
    color: var(--gold);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .eyebrow::before,
  .eyebrow::after { content: "—"; color: var(--gold-soft); margin: 0 0.7em; }

  h1 {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variant-caps: small-caps;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--parchment);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: 0.015em;
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 1.3rem + 3.4vw, 3.5rem);
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .subtitle {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1rem + 0.5vw, 1.3rem);
    max-width: 34rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-align: center;
  }

  hr.rule { border: 0; height: 1px; background: var(--rule); margin: 3rem auto; max-width: 20rem; }

  h2 {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variant-caps: small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--gold);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    margin: 2.4rem 0 0.9rem;
  }
  p { line-height: 1.8; margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }

  blockquote {
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    padding: 0.2rem 0 0.2rem 1.2rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold-soft);
  }
  blockquote p { font-style: italic; color: var(--parchment); margin: 0 0 0.4rem; }
  blockquote cite {
    font-style: normal;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variant-caps: small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--gold-soft);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .lies, .tests { margin: 0 0 1.2rem; padding-left: 1.3rem; }
  .lies li, .tests li { line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .lies { list-style: none; padding-left: 0; }
  .lies li { padding-left: 1.3rem; position: relative; }
  .lies li::before { content: "✦"; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--gold-soft); }
  .tests li::marker { color: var(--gold-soft); }

  .close { font-style: italic; color: var(--parchment); }

  .entries-head { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 1.6rem; }
  .entries { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .entry { margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
  .entry-link {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    background: var(--bg-raise);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 3px;
    transition: border-color 0.2s, background 0.2s;
  }
  .entry-link:hover, .entry-link:focus-visible { border-color: var(--gold); outline: none; }
  .entry-link.is-coming { opacity: 0.6; }

  .entry-n {
    font-family: var(--display);
    color: var(--gold-soft);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    padding-top: 0.15rem;
  }
  .entry-body { flex: 1; }
  .entry-title {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variant-caps: small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--parchment);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
  .entry-work { display: block; color: var(--gold-soft); font-size: 0.86rem; margin-top: 0.15rem; }
  .entry-tag { display: block; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-top: 0.4rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .entry-verses {
    display: block;
    color: var(--gold-soft);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    margin-top: 0.45rem;
  }
  .entry-arrow { color: var(--gold); font-size: 1.1rem; padding-top: 0.15rem; }
  .entry-soon {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variant-caps: small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--gold-soft);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    padding-top: 0.2rem;
  }

  .back-wrap { text-align: center; margin-top: 2.6rem; }
  .back {
    color: var(--gold);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variant-caps: small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  }
  .back:hover { color: var(--parchment); }
  .back:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--gold); outline-offset: 3px; }

  .craft-footer {
    text-align: center;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variant-caps: small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    color: var(--gold);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .entry-link { flex-wrap: wrap; }
  }
</style>
